[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports into one "known" issue: *the parser reads dates
month first, tenants write day first*. That rule comes from
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject): a report is a duplicate when its subject
matches an open ticket's. Nobody has to read the body to merge on subject. Nobody did.

Reading the bodies and running `causes.ts` against the real tenant data shows #4471 is not one
bug. It is three.

<Callout kind="warn">
Same subject line, different bug. The desk's own dedupe rule is what hid this.
</Callout>

## The three problems

#4471 holds 412 unique reports (427 rows in the export, 15 of them re-sent across overlapping
export pages). `causes.ts`'s own `groupByCause` splits them 379 / 33 by cause. A third problem
sits inside that 379, found only by reading bodies, not counted by `causes.ts` at all.

| problem | reports | tenants | what is actually happening |
|---|---|---|---|
| parser reads month-first | **379** (desk's own cause split) | all 11 | Every tenant here writes day-first dates. The shared parser always reads `MM/DD`, so app, email, and `booking-v2`-form submissions come out with month and day swapped. |
| `booking-v3` hint mismatches locale | **33** (desk's own cause split) | alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour | The `booking-v3` form prints a `MM/DD/YYYY` hint to tenants whose locale is day-first. People type what the hint says; the form then parses it the tenant's (day-first) way. Same symptom as the row above, different cause, a different fix. |
| one-day shift, not a swap | **5** (inside the 379 above, not separate from it) | kettle.books, alder.physio, nine.lanterns, pale.harbour, lantern.row | Reports like *"12 May showed as 11 May"* and *"Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday, same meeting"* are off by exactly one day, same month. A month/day swap does not produce that. `causes.ts` has no category for this, so `groupByCause` counts these 5 as `parser` anyway. They are a third, unrelated bug, not a parser miss. |

## How the first two were found

`causes.ts` already splits `parser` from `hint` by tenant locale and form (`groupByCause`). Its
`CauseTable` component renders both rows for #4471 today, and marks whichever one isn't the
ticket's main cause as *"not this ticket — no ticket of its own"*. That table was the start:
the split was already computed, just never given a ticket.

## How the third was found

`causes.ts` has no notion of a one-day shift — it only tells `parser` from `hint`. The desk's own
`desk-notes.json` carries an `oneDayMove` list of five report ids, read differently by whoever
triaged them, but only ever shown as a footnote under whichever cause they happened to land in.
Reading those five bodies: none of them describe a swapped month and day. All of them describe a
date that is one day off, in the same month. They were merged into #4471 because their subject
lines matched, not because they are the same bug:

- `R-41202` (kettle.books, email) — invite said Tuesday 12 May, calendar said Monday 11 May.
- `R-41209` (alder.physio, app) — "Every booking in June is one day off. Only June."
- `R-41236` (nine.lanterns, app) — "The invite arrived before I made the booking."
- `R-41344` (pale.harbour, email) — same meeting, Tuesday in Lisbon, Monday in Toronto.
- `R-41620` (lantern.row, email) — "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday. I moved it myself."

## Tickets filed

One GitHub issue per row above, each carrying its report count and its evidence.

## Engineering update, #4471 closed 05 Oct

| ticket | report count | status | note |
|---|---|---|---|
| parser reads month-first | 379 | **fixed** | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `booking-v3` hint mismatches locale | 33 | **won't fix** | `booking-v3` form retired |
| one-day shift, not a swap | 5 | **open** | not part of this engineering pass — still unexplained |

Tickets closed to match: the parser ticket as completed, the hint ticket as not planned. The
one-day-shift ticket stays open — this update never touched it.

## Lessons

- Subject-line dedupe ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merges fast and
  merges wrong: it can put two different bugs in one ticket as easily as it splits one bug into
  two.
- A table that already shows a second cause (`CauseTable`, on `#4471` today) is a problem without
  a ticket, not a curiosity.
- A footnote (`desk-notes.json`'s `oneDayMove`) is where a third bug hides when nobody reads the
  bodies behind a "known" ticket.

